itted: False` on a terminal BLOCK","reuse.py L227-230: BLOCK-reuse only fires when material_fingerprint AND verified_at_sha match the CURRENT values — i.e. the latest sidecar IS the current run's findings","__init__.py L431-441: idempotent_reuse and verdict_reuse return BEFORE the L564 emit block; L448-459 drift_refresh and L492 cancellation likewise"],"finding":"The fix's core premise — that a terminal plan-review always carries a per-run sidecar_reviewed_at receipt because review_plan() calls sidecar.emit() before the daemon records the run — does not hold for review_plan()'s early-return paths (idempotent_reuse, BLOCK verdict_reuse, drift_refresh, mid-run cancellation), which terminate as completed 'passed' runs WITHOUT reaching the emit block, yet often have a genuinely CURRENT sidecar already on disk.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f92efeb297f46611f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause / actual layer; Fix plan step 4/6; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py L426-493 vs L564; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py L194-260","norm_id":"ncce8872720ac4add","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket in a BLOCK loop with unchanged plan+code: review_plan_start hits verdict_reuse, returns terminal BLOCK with sidecar_emitted=false; gate_status reports findings.readable=false reason='sidecar-not-emitted' even though the latest sidecar is the correct current findings","A ticket with a still-valid PASS attestation: idempotent_reuse returns terminal passed with no fresh emit; caller told findings unreadable though current"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"On the reuse/refresh paths, have reuse.idempotent_reuse / reuse.verdict_reuse / orchestrator.drift_refresh stamp verdict['sidecar_reviewed_at'] with the ns-prefix of the sidecar file they replayed (latest_review_result already locates it; return that filename's timestamp), so the daemon records a receipt that points at the genuinely-current sidecar and findings.readable=true is reported with reason='current-review-result-sidecar'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion asserting that an exact-prefix receipt file that exists but fails to parse (or is an unsupported version) reports findings.readable=false with a defined reason value.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'findings.readable=true only when a file with the exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix exists and parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload'","ACs cover sidecar-missing, current, sidecar-not-emitted, generation-unknown, run-<status> but none covers exists-but-unparseable/unsupported-version"],"finding":"The fix plan requires findings.readable=true only when the exact-prefix file 'parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload' (step 6), but no acceptance criterion exercises the case where an exact-prefix receipt file EXISTS yet fails to parse or is an unsupported version — leaving that branch's reason/readable outcome unspecified and unproven.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc97a3f5969e7bd25","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 6; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n4b357bee18b31993","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A truncated or partially-written exact-prefix REVIEW_RESULT file is present when gate_status is polled","A future/unsupported plan_review_result version is written to the exact-prefix path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: seed the exact sidecar_reviewed_at-prefix file with unparseable/unsupported-version content and assert findings.readable=false with an explicit reason (e.g. reason=\"review-result-unreadable\"), and enumerate that reason in step 6.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion asserting that a prefix-matching but unparseable / unsupported-schema-version REVIEW_RESULT reports findings.readable=false with a defined reason.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'findings.readable=true only when a file with the exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix exists and parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload.'","The Acceptance Criteria cover missing sidecar, present current sidecar, sidecar_emitted=false, legacy-no-receipt, and non-terminal states, but none covers a prefix-matching-but-unparseable/unsupported-version payload."],"finding":"The readability rule requires a matching-prefix file that also 'parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload', but no acceptance criterion exercises the parse-failure branch — a file with the exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix that is corrupt/unparseable or an unsupported schema version. That failure arm of the new logic ships untested.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4963c08a6b4f02f1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 6 / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n77638ed06eb5eec4","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sidecar file with the exact receipt prefix is written but truncated or written under a future/unsupported schema version; the parse-guard branch decides readable=false with an unspecified reason, and no test proves that behavior."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: write a file with the exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix but malformed JSON / an unsupported plan_review_result_v* version, and assert readable=false with the intended reason (e.g. review-result-generation-unknown or a dedicated parse-failure reason).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the value vocabulary for the `findings.sidecar_type` field (e.g. the exact constant(s) it emits for a plan-review job) and pin it in an acceptance criterion.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 5 lists the emitted fields: 'findings for plan-review jobs: sidecar_type, readable, reason, reviewed_at, latest_reviewed_at, and legacy diagnostic job_started_at' — but no section defines what values sidecar_type takes.","search_files for 'sidecar_type' across src/rebar returns (no matches): the field is newly introduced by this plan, so its vocabulary is not inheritable from existing code.","No acceptance criterion references sidecar_type; every AC pins `reason` and `readable` but none constrains sidecar_type's value(s)."],"finding":"The `findings` block emits a `sidecar_type` field whose value vocabulary is never defined in the plan; a polling consumer cannot know what values it can hold.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe0e4cc7d401b1872","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 5 (`gate_status(job_id)` adds `findings` … `sidecar_type`); Scope / file impact: src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","norm_id":"n3bb5963e477701c4","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller/agent branches on findings.sidecar_type to distinguish plan-review from other gate findings but has no defined value set to match against.","A test author cannot assert the emitted sidecar_type value because the plan states none."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the concrete sidecar_type value(s) — e.g. sidecar_type=\"REVIEW_RESULT\" for plan-review jobs — in Fix plan step 5 and assert it in the readable=true / readable=false ACs.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the new gate_runs.py readability check reuses/extends sidecar.py's prefix-walk + schema-guard (and lifts the plan_review_result_v1/v2 accepted-schema set into one shared constant) rather than adding a fourth inline copy of the schema tuple.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 6: 'a file with the exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix exists and parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload'","sidecar.py latest_review_result/all_review_results already do `for fname in reversed(files)` prefix walks with `payload.get('schema') in ('plan_review_result_v1','plan_review_result_v2')` — the schema tuple is inline-literaled at 3 sites, not a shared constant","The existing readers are newest-by-ticket (the plan's own root cause: 'sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket) is newest-by-ticket, not job-scoped') so a job-scoped reader IS justified — the concern is DRY, not rebuild-vs-extend NIH"],"finding":"The plan adds a job-scoped 'exact sidecar_reviewed_at prefix + plan_review_result_v1/v2 schema' readability check in gate_runs.py, but sidecar.py already implements prefix-walking + the identical v1/v2 schema guard (latest_review_result/all_review_results). The v1/v2 tuple is already re-literaled three times in sidecar.py; the plan risks a fourth inline copy and does not say whether the new reader shares that schema constant or reuses the existing walk logic.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe04c087a0e53d2ae","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 6 + Scope/file impact: src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","norm_id":"nc87e6768cbf5817c","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future schema bump (v3) must be updated in 4 places instead of 1, and an omitted site silently mis-classifies findings as unreadable"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a small exact-prefix reader beside the existing sidecar readers in sidecar.py (e.g. review_result_for_receipt(ticket_id, reviewed_at)) that shares a single `_SUPPORTED_SCHEMAS` constant with latest_review_result/all_review_results; have gate_runs.py call it, keeping the readability logic out of the index module.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the status values that interpolate into `run-<status>` and specify whether `stale-running` is a keep-polling reason or a distinct terminal-unavailable finding.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.465,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["The plan calls run-<status> 'the non-terminal keep-polling state' but never enumerates which status values fill <status>.","gate_runs._resolve_status returns running / attaching / stale-running for non-terminal records; stale-running denotes a CRASHED leader (daemon no longer active past the grace window), for which 'keep polling' is semantically wrong — yet the plan folds all non-terminal states under run-<status>.","The AC 'assert non-terminal plan-review runs report … reason=\"run-<status>\"' tests a placeholder, not a defined value set."],"finding":"The `run-<status>` non-terminal reason interpolates a status value whose domain is not enumerated, and it is unclear whether the crashed-leader `stale-running` status is treated as a keep-polling state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f09ca0b54483631c8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Disposition paragraph ('`run-<status>` is the non-terminal keep-polling state'); AC line 'non-terminal plan-review runs report … reason=\"run-<status>\"'","norm_id":"n38c9c90f45dfb720","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller polls a stale-running (dead-daemon) job and, seeing reason=run-stale-running described as keep-polling, loops forever against a job that will never settle."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"List the non-terminal statuses (running, attaching) that yield run-<status>, and state explicitly how stale-running maps (either a distinct terminal-unavailable reason or an enumerated run-<status> value with defined caller semantics).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_a